.TH SH-DOCS 1 "2026-09-28" "sh-docs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sh\-docs \- generate Markdown API documentation from shell doc comments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sh\-docs
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sh\-docs
reads a shell script and writes GitHub\-flavored Markdown describing it.
It parses the annotations in the file header and in the comment block above
each function definition, and renders a document with a navigation block, an
overview, a highlight list of the documented functions, and a reference section
with tables for arguments, options, environment variables, exit codes and
streams.
.PP
\fIFILE\fR defaults to standard input, and the document is written to standard
output unless
.B \-\-output
is given.
.PP
The annotation language is documented in the project README. In short, the file
header takes
.BR @file / @name ,
.BR @brief ,
.BR @description ,
.BR @usage ,
.BR @env ,
.BR @see ,
.BR @tip ,
.B @deprecated
and
.BR @license ,
and a function takes
.BR @description ,
.BR @section ,
.BR @example ,
.BR @arg ,
.BR @option ,
.BR @env ,
.BR @set ,
.BR @exitcode ,
.BR @stdin ,
.BR @stdout ,
.BR @stderr ,
.BR @noargs ,
.BR @note ,
.BR @tip ,
.BR @see ,
.B @deprecated
and
.BR @internal .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the document to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-\-src\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Directory the documented sources live in. Default: \fBsrc\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-doc\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Directory the generated documents live in, used to resolve relative links.
Default: \fBdocs\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-root\-files " \fILIST\fR"
Comma\-separated sources that sit at the repository root instead of inside
\fB\-\-src\-dir\fR. Default: \fBinit.sh\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-source\-path " \fIPATH\fR"
Path of the documented source relative to the repository root. Overrides
\fB\-\-src\-dir\fR and \fB\-\-root\-files\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-link\-dirs " \fILIST\fR"
Comma\-separated path prefixes that \fB@see\fR entries are resolved as paths
rather than as anchors. Default: \fBdocs,example,src,scripts\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-example\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Scan \fIDIR\fR for example scripts that mention a documented function and list
them under "Related examples". Scanning is off by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-example\-prefix " \fIDIR\fR"
Prefix the scanned examples are linked under. Default: \fBexample\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SH_DOCS_AWK
Path of the awk program. Defaults to
.I sh\-docs.awk
next to the
.B sh\-docs
script.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The document was generated.
.TP
.B 1
The invocation was invalid, the input could not be read, or awk failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Generate a document for one module:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sh\-docs < src/strings.sh > docs/strings.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Document a module that lives outside the default layout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sh\-docs \-\-source\-path lib/text/strings.sh lib/text/strings.sh \-o docs/strings.md
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gawk (1),
.BR shdoc (1)
